-- Phone number detection that requires valid numbers. By default the phone filter
-- reports any candidate whose length is possible for a region (leniency POSSIBLE),
-- which can match short numeric identifiers or years. Set `leniency` to VALID to
-- keep only numbers that are valid under the region's numbering plan; STRICT_GROUPING
-- and EXACT_GROUPING also constrain how the digits are grouped. Set through the
-- existing OPTIONS passthrough; no grammar change. Added to schema 1.3.0 in place
-- (additive). Compiles to phone-leniency.json.

POLICY phone_leniency;

REDACT PHONE_NUMBER WITH REDACT OPTIONS (region = ['US', 'GB', 'DE'], leniency = 'VALID');
